#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Mock `adb` (Android Debug Bridge) for the linux-drills training image.

There is no real device: this script plays the adb client, the adb server and a Qualcomm QCS6490
"Facility Hub" running Android 13.  Everything it knows lives in /var/lib/mock-adb/ (root-owned; when
run as another user the script re-executes itself through `sudo -n`, so a scenario's state is not
casually editable and no world-writable files are needed).

STATE  /var/lib/mock-adb/state.json is a *partial* JSON document.  On every call it is deep-merged over
the built-in healthy default (dicts merge, lists/scalars replace) and the full result is written back.
A scenario's break.sh therefore only writes the keys it wants to change.  Keys:

  server.running          adb server (daemon) up?  False => the next call prints the "* daemon not running" lines
  usb_devices             physical USB devices: [{serial, state, usb}]   state: device|offline|unauthorized|no permissions
  devices                 the SERVER's transport table: [{serial, transport: usb|tcp, state, tid}]
                          (usb entries are re-derived from usb_devices while the server runs; tcp entries are
                          authoritative, which is how a stale 'offline' entry survives until kill-server/disconnect)
  hosts                   what answers on the LAN: {"10.50.0.77": {hub: true, ports: {"5555": true}, authorized: true}}
                          (unknown host => connect times out; known host, closed port => connection refused)
  reboot                  {until: epoch} while the hub is rebooting (10 s)
  hub.boot_epoch          when the hub last booted
  hub.wan_up              wired uplink works? (`adb shell ping` succeeds if wan_up or the cellular data link is up)
  hub.props               static getprop values (gsm.* are DERIVED, see below)
  hub.settings.{global,secure,system}   `settings get/put`.  airplane_mode_on / mobile_data live in global
  hub.radio               {airplane: effective modem-off flag, sim: present|absent|pin_required, coverage: bool}
                          NOTE: `settings put global airplane_mode_on 0` changes only the setting; the radio follows
                          `cmd connectivity airplane-mode ...` or `am broadcast -a android.intent.action.AIRPLANE_MODE`
  hub.packages.<pkg>      {permissions: {perm: {granted, runtime, flags}}, requires: [perms needed to start],
                           persistent, running, pid, next_restart (epoch), restart_delay (s), ...}
                          A persistent package that is not running is (re)started when next_restart passes; if a
                          required permission is missing it crashes (FATAL EXCEPTION in logcat) and the restart
                          delay grows x4 up to 1 h, exactly like ActivityManager's crashed-service backoff.
                          `am force-stop` resets the backoff and restarts it at once; `pm grant` alone does not.
  logcat.<buf>.txt        logcat ring buffers (main system radio events crash) in threadtime format

DERIVED (never stored, computed from the above on every call): gsm.sim.state, gsm.network.type, telephony
registry service/data state, rmnet_data0 up/down, the device list.

ADMIN interface for break.sh / check.sh (root; undocumented in `adb help`):
  adb --mock get PATH          print a value; PATH is '/'-separated, e.g.  hub/packages/com.facility.camerad/running
                               or derived/sim_state  derived/devices  derived/airplane  derived/data_conn_state
  adb --mock set PATH JSON     e.g.  adb --mock set hub/settings/global/airplane_mode_on '"1"'
  adb --mock log BUF AGO_S PID TID LVL TAG MSG...   append a threadtime line dated AGO_S seconds ago
  adb --mock noise BUF N SPAN_S                     N generic background lines spread over the last SPAN_S seconds
  adb --mock tick | dump | reset
"""
